FAIL  plan review by gemini-3.8-flash-high (agy)
    root_cause    ok    The plan addresses root cause rather than symptoms: it enforces characterising actual simulator behavior first through the public seam exportIosVideoOverlay without speculative production code rewrites, requires capturing genuine findings before proposing a fix, and explicitly forbids weak fallback branches (such as accepting refusal as a pass).
    tests         FAIL  The planned tests will not run cleanly due to a fatal crash in the test helper: probe(path) unconditionally executes CFRetain on the return value of CMFormatDescriptionGetExtension. When an extension key is absent (as is always the case for SDR source.mp4, and for exported files that drop transfer tags), CFRetain(NULL) causes an immediate native runtime abort (SIGABRT), crashing the test runner rather than failing an assertion. Additionally, the test fails to assert exported track dimensions, codec subtype (hvc1), and color primaries required by Spec Acceptance Criterion 2.
    code_fit      FAIL  Contradicts CoreFoundation API contract at IosVideoOverlayExporterTest.kt:137-138 where CFRetain(NULL) causes a fatal abort when format description extensions are absent (e.g. for SDR fixtures and downgraded outputs). It also contradicts existing test assertion patterns by omitting dimension assertions and artifact copying to SNAPVAULT_TEST_OUTPUTS.
    completeness  FAIL  The plan and accompanying test draft miss multiple requirements: Spec Criterion 1 (full SHA-256 hashes missing from video-overlay/README.md:42 and no sha256 checksum file in docs/audits/evidence/native-2026-11-10/), Spec Criterion 2 (exported file assertions omit dimensions, codec subtype hvc1, and color primaries ITU_R_2020), and Spec Criterion 6 (exported HDR outputs are not saved to SNAPVAULT_TEST_OUTPUTS).
    [blocker] composeApp/src/iosTest/kotlin/com/najdev/snapvault/metadata/IosVideoOverlayExporterTest.kt:137-138 — Helper extension(key) calls CFRetain(CMFormatDescriptionGetExtension(description, key)) unconditionally. In Apple CoreFoundation, passing NULL to CFRetain triggers an immediate fatal assertion/abort. This will crash the test process whenever an extension is absent, including for SDR fixture source.mp4 in probe(sdr.source), in anSdrSourceStaysSdrAfterExport, and whenever an exported file lacks transfer-function or color tags. It must null-check the pointer before calling CFRetain.
    [major] composeApp/src/iosTest/kotlin/com/najdev/snapvault/metadata/IosVideoOverlayExporterTest.kt:104-118 — hdrSourcesKeepTheirTransferFunctionThroughExport fails to assert dimensions, codec subtype (HEVC/hvc1), and color primaries on the exported file, violating Spec Acceptance Criterion 2. While StreamProbe reads codec and primaries, they are only printed in println without assertions, and dimensions (naturalSize) are not checked at all. Without asserting out.codec == HEVC, bit depth inference is incomplete.
    [major] composeApp/src/iosTest/resources/video-overlay/README.md:42 — Plan Step 1 claims full metadata and hashes are documented in video-overlay/README.md and present in docs/audits/evidence/native-2026-11-10/. In reality, line 42 of video-overlay/README.md only contains truncated hashes (57e2c0a9…a489, 9108eb1f…28f9), and no SHA-256 hash file exists in docs/audits/evidence/native-2026-11-10/, violating Spec Acceptance Criterion 1.
    [minor] composeApp/src/iosTest/kotlin/com/najdev/snapvault/metadata/IosVideoOverlayExporterTest.kt:186-193 — Unlike verifyExport, hdrSourcesKeepTheirTransferFunctionThroughExport deletes fixture.output immediately in its finally block without copying it to SNAPVAULT_TEST_OUTPUTS, preventing the exported native HDR files from being inspected or archived for evidence under Spec Acceptance Criterion 6.
    simpler: Guard the CoreFoundation retain in extension with a null check (val ext = CMFormatDescriptionGetExtension(description, key) ?: return null; return CFBridgingRelease(platform.CoreFoundation.CFRetain(ext)) as? String), and update hdrSourcesKeepTheirTransferFunctionThroughExport to incorporate structural checks and artifact saving from verifyExport while asserting out.codec == HEVC, out.transfer == transfer, out.primaries == 'ITU_R_2020', and out.hdrCharacteristic.
    summary: The plan correctly prioritizes characterizing real simulator exporter behavior before changing production code, but the proposed implementation contains a blocker bug (CFRetain(NULL) crash on missing extensions in the test probe helper), major test coverage gaps (missing dimensions, codec subtype, and primaries assertions on the exported file required by Spec Criterion 2), and missing SHA-256 fixture documentation in video-overlay/README.md and docs/audits/evidence/native-2026-11-10/.
